<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 29.13 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 29.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 21 points to 29.13 percent and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     29.34	    29.13		  -  21 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     30.10	    28.99		  - 111 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    29.30	    28.02		  - 128 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     28.63	    27.78		  -  85 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EDT.</p>
<p>- Patricia Lezama, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289554</p>
